<div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
  <%= render layout: "components/ui/page_header",
             locals: { title: "Add new student" } do %><% end %>

  <%= form_with model: [@classroom, @student], local: true, class: "space-y-6" do |f| %>
    <% if @student.errors.any? %>
      <%# "rounded-smrelative" - rounded-sm and relative fused into one token, so the browser
          applied neither. Tokens: red-50 tint with a red-200 hairline and red-700 ink, matching
          the callout's alert shape, at the rounded-2xl panel radius. %>
      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-red-200 bg-red-50 px-4 py-3 text-red-700" role="alert">
        <strong class="font-bold">Error:</strong>
        <ul>
          <% @student.errors.full_messages.each do |message| %>
            <li><%= message %></li>
          <% end %>
        </ul>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <div class="bg-white shadow-sm overflow-hidden lg:rounded-md">
      <div class="px-4 py-5 lg:p-6">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-6 gap-6">
          <%# `users.name` has existed the whole time and `User#display_name` prefers it, but
              nothing ever collected it - so every student's name was nil and every screen fell back to a
              lowercased username. Reported as "why are all the student names lowercase": they were not
              names. Required here, on the form, rather than on every create: bulk CSV import takes a
              username and a classroom id and nothing else, so a model-wide requirement would fail every
              row of a class being onboarded. See Student. %>
          <div class="col-span-6 lg:col-span-4">
            <%= f.label :name, class: "tw-label-primary" do %>
              Full name<span class="required-indicator">*</span>
            <% end %>
            <%= f.text_field :name,
                             class: "tw-input-primary",
                             required: true,
                             placeholder: "e.g., Jordan Smith" %>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">
              Shown instead of the username wherever this student appears. A roster of usernames alone is
              hard to read.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="col-span-6 lg:col-span-4">
            <%= f.label :username, class: "tw-label-primary" %>
            <%= f.text_field :username, class: "tw-input-primary", required: true, placeholder: "e.g., john_doe" %>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">
              What the student signs in with. A password is generated automatically.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="px-4 py-3 bg-slate-50 text-right lg:px-6">
        <%= f.submit "Create student", class: "tw-btn-primary" %>
        <%= link_to "Cancel", classroom_path(@classroom), class: "tw-btn-secondary ml-3" %>
      </div>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
